window.__LDNDRC_PAGES = Object.assign(window.__LDNDRC_PAGES || {}, {"hardware-gate":"<p>Not every laptop should become a <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"host\" tabindex=\"0\">Host</span>. The gate is a deterministic check run before anything is installed, so a weak machine is never offered a <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"k3s\" tabindex=\"0\">K3s</span> agent it cannot carry.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-bar\">The bar</h2><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Resource</th>\n<th>Minimum</th>\n<th>Why</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>CPU cores</td>\n<td>8</td>\n<td>A <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"session\" tabindex=\"0\">session</span> <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"pod\" tabindex=\"0\">pod</span> runs an editor, a desktop, <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"gazebo\" tabindex=\"0\">Gazebo</span>, and ROS</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>RAM</td>\n<td>16 GB</td>\n<td><span class=\"term\" data-term=\"gazebo\" tabindex=\"0\">Gazebo</span> plus <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"dds\" tabindex=\"0\">DDS</span> plus the browser tooling</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>GPU</td>\n<td>NVIDIA</td>\n<td>The <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"workspace-image\" tabindex=\"0\">workspace image</span> requests <code>nvidia.com/gpu: 1</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Disk</td>\n<td>~25 GB free</td>\n<td>The image is roughly 10 GB, imported per <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"node\" tabindex=\"0\">node</span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<h2 id=\"the-verdicts\">The verdicts</h2><div class=\"code term\" data-lang=\"text\"><span class=\"lang-tag\">text</span><button class=\"copy\" data-copy aria-label=\"Copy code\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-copy\"/></svg></button><pre><code class=\"hljs language-text\">High-end laptop detected. Joining as HOST.\nLow-end laptop detected. Staying a Guest — use the browser.</code></pre></div><p>There is no third option and no manual override in the normal path. That is intentional: a <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"host\" tabindex=\"0\">Host</span> that cannot carry a <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"session\" tabindex=\"0\">session</span> makes the whole workshop worse for one student, silently.</p>\n<h2 id=\"testing-the-gate-without-hardware\">Testing the gate without hardware</h2><p>The detection logic is separated from the install so it can be exercised in two seconds:</p>\n<div class=\"code term\" data-lang=\"bash\"><span class=\"lang-tag\">bash</span><button class=\"copy\" data-copy aria-label=\"Copy code\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-copy\"/></svg></button><pre><code class=\"hljs language-bash\">./test-join.sh\nTEST_CPU=12 TEST_RAM=16 TEST_GPU=nvidia ./join-cluster.sh</code></pre></div><p><code>TEST_*</code> overrides exist because CI and developer machines rarely look like workshop laptops. They change only the input to the decision, not the decision itself.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-real-lesson\">The real lesson</h2><p>The gate is deliberately conservative. A laptop with 15 GB of RAM is a <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"guest\" tabindex=\"0\">Guest</span> even though it would probably cope. Being wrong in that direction costs one unused machine. Being wrong in the other direction costs a student their <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"session\" tabindex=\"0\">session</span> in the middle of a lesson.</p>\n<h2 id=\"how-it-connects\">How it connects</h2><ul>\n<li>The gate decides whether a laptop can even reach <a href=\"#/nodes-api\" class=\"topic-link\">Register, approve, poll</a>&#39;s approval step as a <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"host\" tabindex=\"0\">Host</span>.</li>\n<li>It is why the join binary can say &quot;you cannot join&quot; before downloading anything — see <a href=\"#/join-binary\" class=\"topic-link\">The join binary</a>.</li>\n<li>GPU capacity is then shared with <a href=\"#/gpu-timeslicing\" class=\"topic-link\">Time-slicing one GPU</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"check-it-yourself\">Check it yourself</h2><div class=\"code term\" data-lang=\"bash\"><span class=\"lang-tag\">bash</span><button class=\"copy\" data-copy aria-label=\"Copy code\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-copy\"/></svg></button><pre><code class=\"hljs language-bash\">TEST_CPU=12 TEST_RAM=16 TEST_GPU=nvidia ./join-cluster.sh\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\"># High-end laptop detected. Joining as HOST.</span></code></pre></div>","gpu-timeslicing":"<p>A consumer GeForce cannot be partitioned the way a datacentre card can. <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"gpu-timeslicing\" tabindex=\"0\">Time-slicing</span> fakes it: the NVIDIA device plugin advertises several logical GPUs on one physical card, and the scheduler hands them out as if they were separate.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-shape\">The shape</h2><ul>\n<li>Install the NVIDIA GPU <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"operator\" tabindex=\"0\">Operator</span>.</li>\n<li>Patch the <code>ClusterPolicy</code> with a <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"gpu-timeslicing\" tabindex=\"0\">time-slicing</span> <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"configmap\" tabindex=\"0\">ConfigMap</span> (<code>replicas: 4</code>).</li>\n<li><span class=\"term\" data-term=\"session\" tabindex=\"0\">Session</span> <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"pod\" tabindex=\"0\">pods</span> request <code>nvidia.com/gpu: 1</code> each.</li>\n<li>Set <code>SESSION_GPU_LIMIT=1</code> in the panel.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The result is up to four <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"session\" tabindex=\"0\">session</span> <span class=\"term\" data-term=\"pod\" tabindex=\"0\">pods</span> per physical GPU, sharing it by time rather than memory. Four students on one gaming laptop is the whole economic argument for the platform.</p>\n<h2 id=\"the-honest-caveat\">The honest caveat</h2><p>Time-sliced GPUs do not isolate memory. One student&#39;s oversized scene can push another&#39;s frame rate down. For a workshop that is acceptable; for an exam it would not be. The roadmap&#39;s R7 track is where limits and dashboards would go.</p>\n<h2 id=\"check-it-yourself\">Check it yourself</h2><div class=\"code term\" data-lang=\"bash\"><span class=\"lang-tag\">bash</span><button class=\"copy\" data-copy aria-label=\"Copy code\"><svg aria-hidden=\"true\"><use href=\"#i-copy\"/></svg></button><pre><code class=\"hljs language-bash\">kubectl get nodes -o jsonpath=<span class=\"hljs-string\">&#x27;{.items[*].status.allocatable.nvidia\\.com/gpu}&#x27;</span>\n<span class=\"hljs-comment\"># 4 on a time-sliced single-GPU Host</span></code></pre></div>"});
